+## ADDED Requirements
+### Requirement: Exhaustive teardown cleanup
+Flask SHALL invoke every registered request or application-context teardown
+callback, followed by that phase's tearing-down signal, when the phase runs.
+If one or more of those actions raises, Flask SHALL complete the phase before
+raising the collected failures. On Python versions with exception-group
+support, all collected failures SHALL be preserved in an exception group; on
+older supported Python versions, Flask MAY raise the first collected failure.
+
+#### Scenario: Teardown callback fails
+- WHEN a teardown callback raises and later callbacks or the phase signal are registered
+- THEN Flask invokes the later callbacks and signal before propagating teardown failure
+
+#### Scenario: Context teardown failure
+- WHEN request or application-context teardown raises while its context is popped
+- THEN the application's context-local state is restored before the failure escapes
